## Context

Promotion currently identifies entries by filename equality, which yields one
candidate. A lexical pass over slug words finds roughly 43 candidate pairs of
which 17–21 are genuine — so the mechanism is not short of material, it is
short of a way to recognise it. About half of any lexical pass is noise, which
is why confirmation is part of this ticket rather than an afterthought.

Design reference: defect 2, "What the model decides, and what it must not", and
ticket T4 in `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`.

## Relevant files

- `skills/dream/SKILL.md` — the consolidation pass
- `skills/dream/provenance.py` — promotion candidacy and the live-body walker

## Actions

1. Pool the project directories **and the harness tier**. The harness is a
   project like any other here: it has direct writes, it is compared against,
   and it takes part in the pairs the pass finds. The one asymmetry is a
   direction — promotion moves up into it and never back out — which settles in
   advance what happens when a pair straddles the tiers: the harness copy
   survives, the project copy is tombstoned, nothing new is created.
2. Group candidates mechanically. Grouping is not the judgment step.
3. Let a model decide whether a group is one lesson and write the merged body,
   naming what it supersedes. **It decides nothing about retention** — not what
   ranks, not what expires, not what is still true. Those stay deterministic,
   which is what keeps the index reproducible from the store alone.
4. Route merges into the harness tier through review. It is the only operation
   that replaces text with different text, it reaches every session, and it is
   where both silent loss and poisoning would enter.
5. Record the model's identity and its prompt in the run's provenance, beside
   the embedding model's, so a later reader can tell why a merge looks as it
   does.
6. Report near-miss pairs — similar enough to suspect, different enough not to
   merge — as contradiction candidates. The similarity is already computed.
7. Record the body count and the pass's own wall-clock duration. Growth gets an
   **alarm, not a cap**: a file-count ceiling would be a deletion mechanism, and
   what actually degrades is this pass, not the corpus.
8. Trigger `0910`'s regeneration when the pass changes a directory.

## Test

Red first: a known-genuine pair is surfaced; a known lexical false positive
(`dropna_before_merge` / `rebase_before_merge` is one) is not merged; a pair
straddling project and harness tiers resolves by tombstoning the project copy.

## Verification

- [ ] Candidates rise from 1 to the 17–21 genuine pairs
- [ ] No merge applies without confirmation
- [ ] Promoted slugs leave no body counted live (depends on `0908`)
- [ ] The run's provenance carries model identity, prompt, body count, duration

## Invariants

- Nothing is deleted. Merged originals are tombstoned and remain readable, which
  is what makes a wrong merge recoverable rather than fatal.
- The harness tier is never a promotion *destination for removal*: entries move
  up into it and stop.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Genuine cross-project pairs surfaced, lexical false positives rejected
      before any merge
- [ ] The harness tier participates on the same footing, promotion one-way
- [ ] Promotion tombstones the project copies
- [ ] Near-miss pairs reported as contradiction candidates
- [ ] Corpus size and pass duration recorded; no file-count cap introduced
